{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 89, :comments ["The sense of <b>ובבא משה</b>. It is possible that the beginning of the speech — namely ויקרא אל משה — was when the dedication was completed. All the precise grammarians say that מדבר is a binyan hitpa'el form and the tav is assimilated. In my opinion it is a noun, like הנה לא ידעתי דבר, and the mem stands in place of מן for the rule of the language." "The sense of <b>וישמע</b>: that he alone heard the voice, and no one who was in the Tent of Meeting outside the curtain would hear it. This too is correct, for HaShem added to the perception of his ears just as He added to the sight of the lad Elisha's eyes, and likewise ויגל ה' את עיני בלעם." "<b>וידבר אליו</b>. Such was always the manner of the speech."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:48.319395864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}